# One line. Run from the repo root by `orgasmic verify TASK-4YC8E`.
#
# Two named tests, one per half of the defect, and nothing else:
#
#   every_supported_pair_accepts_the_daemons_dual_key_effort_config
#     (orgasmic-drivers lib) — replays the exact driver config `api.rs` composes
#     for a dispatch, effort under both key names, through the production
#     validation path `driver_for_mode_harness(mode, harness).validate(..)`, for
#     every supported pair. Deserialization only: no harness, no provider, no
#     process, no spend. A real hermes dispatch would reach a real provider,
#     which is why the confirmation is hermetic.
#
#   driver_validate_400_carries_the_drivers_own_message
#     (orgasmic-daemon lib) — the 400 that rejection produces must name the
#     adapter and carry the driver's own message.
#
# `--no-fail-fast` so both halves report; without it cargo stops at the first
# failing binary and the drivers half never runs. `--skip` on the billed drivers
# test is required by `orgasmic verify` for anything touching that suite.
env -u ORGASMIC_RUN_ID -u ORGASMIC_HOME cargo test --no-fail-fast -p orgasmic-drivers -p orgasmic-daemon --lib -- every_supported_pair_accepts_the_daemons_dual_key_effort_config driver_validate_400_carries_the_drivers_own_message --skip legacy_drivers_and_explicit_pairs_emit_equivalent_start_events
